@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide methods
hide circle
title Iteration II — resource detail (subset of domain-model)
class MedicalService {
  name
  fee
  requiresReferral
}
class ResourceRequirement {
  resourceKind
  quantity
}
class Resource {
  name
  kind: room / equipment / role
}
class ClinicLocation {
  name
  address
  phone
}
class Appointment {
  status
  arrivalTime
}
class TimeSlot {
  date
  startTime
  endTime
  status: OPEN / BOOKED
}
MedicalService "1" -- "0..*" ResourceRequirement : requires
ResourceRequirement "0..*" -- "0..*" Resource : can be satisfied by
ClinicLocation "1" -- "0..*" Resource : provides predefined units
Appointment "0..*" -- "0..*" Resource : allocates for its interval
Appointment "0..*" -- "1" TimeSlot : assigned to (history retained)
Appointment "0..*" -- "1" MedicalService : is for
TimeSlot "0..*" -- "1" ClinicLocation : applies at
note bottom of Resource
  Each resource is one predefined unit.
  Requirements restrict allowed units, kind and quantity.
  Human resources represent roles, not named personnel.
  Units cannot have overlapping active allocations.
  Cancellation breaks allocation links, freeing the units.
end note
@enduml
